## Per-Finding Evidence & Remediation

### 1. `/usr/bin/php8.3` (LIKELY_VULNERABLE)

- **Priority:** `P2`
- **SAPI:** `cli`
- **Upstream Version:** `8.3.35`
- **Package:** `php8.3-cli` (`2:8.3.35-1+deb12u1`, manager: `deb`)
- **Distribution:** `debian 12`
- **Reason:** upstream version 8.3.35 < 8.3.36 on distro-managed package (backports possible)
- **Mitigation Status:** `CVE-2026-109618=NONE_AVAILABLE, CVE-2026-109619=APPLIED`

#### Evidence

- `pkg_db: /var/lib/dpkg/status => php8.3-cli 2:8.3.35-1+deb12u1 (deb)`
- `ini:session.upload_progress.enabled=0 (source: /etc/php/8.3/cli/php.ini:1)`

#### Recommended Remediation

- Upgrade PHP on branch 8.3 to >= 8.3.36.
- Temporary configuration mitigation diff (applies to CVE-2026-109619 only; not a fix):

```diff
--- a/php.ini
+++ b/php.ini
-session.upload_progress.enabled = 1
+session.upload_progress.enabled = 0
```


**Commands (display only):**
- Update container base image: `bump the base image tag to 8.3.36`

**Restart Hints:**
- reload php-fpm or Apache if web SAPIs share this PHP installation

> WARNING: A configuration mitigation is a temporary risk reduction only and is NOT a fix. CVE-2026-109618 has no known configuration mitigation; upgrading PHP is required.

### 2. `/usr/sbin/php-fpm8.3` (LIKELY_VULNERABLE)

- **Priority:** `P0`
- **SAPI:** `fpm`
- **Upstream Version:** `8.3.35`
- **Package:** `php8.3-fpm` (`2:8.3.35-1+deb12u1`, manager: `deb`)
- **Distribution:** `debian 12`
- **Reason:** upstream version 8.3.35 < 8.3.36 on distro-managed package (backports possible)
- **Mitigation Status:** `CVE-2026-109618=NONE_AVAILABLE, CVE-2026-109619=APPLIED`

#### Evidence

- `pkg_db: /var/lib/dpkg/status => php8.3-fpm 2:8.3.35-1+deb12u1 (deb)`
- `pool dir found by default location`
- `ini:session.upload_progress.enabled=0 (source: /etc/php/8.3/fpm/pool.d/www.conf (php_admin_value) at /etc/php/8.3/fpm/pool.d/www.conf:2)`

#### Recommended Remediation

- Upgrade PHP on branch 8.3 to >= 8.3.36.
- Temporary configuration mitigation diff (applies to CVE-2026-109619 only; not a fix):

```diff
--- a/php.ini
+++ b/php.ini
-session.upload_progress.enabled = 1
+session.upload_progress.enabled = 0
--- a/pool.d/www.conf
+++ b/pool.d/www.conf
+php_admin_value[session.upload_progress.enabled] = 0
```


**Commands (display only):**
- Update container base image: `bump the base image tag to 8.3.36`

**Restart Hints:**
- reload php-fpm (e.g. systemctl reload php-fpm)

> WARNING: A configuration mitigation is a temporary risk reduction only and is NOT a fix. CVE-2026-109618 has no known configuration mitigation; upgrading PHP is required.

## Limitations & Assessment Notes

- **Read-Only Discovery:** `php2shell-check` performs passive version and configuration inspection without sending exploit payloads or executing untrusted binaries.
- **Configuration Mitigations:** INI or FPM pool mitigations apply only to `CVE-2026-109619` and never alter the vulnerability verdict. `CVE-2026-109618` has no known configuration mitigation.
- **Vendor Backports:** When `advisory.verified` is `false` or distribution backport versions are not listed in `distro_fixes`, distro-managed packages below the upstream fix version are reported as `LIKELY_VULNERABLE`.
